================================================================
INFRASTRUCTURE OBSERVATIONS
================================================================

Bead-tracker contention
  The `.beads/issues.jsonl` + internal SQLite database became a hot
  contention point as 7 concurrent panes each ran `br list / show /
  update / close` plus the auto-flush job. `br_retry.sh` timeouts at
  10s were hit multiple times. The system stayed functional but query
  latency spiked. For larger swarms (>7), the bead tracker likely
  needs read-replica or query coalescing.

.git/index.lock collisions
  Hit 7 times across ~45 minutes. Each recovery: backup to /tmp +
  `rm .git/index.lock` after `pgrep "git "` confirmed no live writer.
  The race-safe `git commit --only PATH` pattern from AGENTS.md memory
  was followed by panes but doesn't fully eliminate the acquisition
  race when bursts of 4-5 concurrent commits land.

Cron triage filter quality
  The convergence filter
  `[.[] | select(.priority <= 2 and .issue_type != "epic" and
   (.id | startswith("bd-3usjw.11.1") | not))]`
  cleanly separated tractable work from external-dep blocked work.
  Without that filter, the swarm would have ground forever on
  path-dep publishing beads it cannot unblock.

Stuck-pane patterns
  Two long-running in_progress holds (bd-21xbi.1 lexical-RAM at
  ~30min, bd-3n7ms search bloom at 50+ min) blocked their respective
  panes for the entire session. Neither agent shipped; both were left
  in_progress. Per OC-003 ladder these would normally trigger
  smart-restart, but they may be in genuine deep work — the user's
  next session can decide whether to retire them or carry forward.

